    | 41  | %\nL65: Operating margin  |    | 85  | %  |    | 83  | %  |    | 25  | %\nL66:    |    |    |\nL67: Mobile and Client Business Unit  |    |    |\nL68: Revenue  | $  | 13,114  |    | $  | 11,521  |    | $  | 3,760  |\nL69: Gross margin  |    | 90  | %  |    | 87  | %  |    | 36  | %\nL70: Operating margin  |    | 88  | %  |    | 86  | %  |    | 29  | %\nL71:    |    |    |\nL72: Automotive and Embedded Business Unit  |    |    |\nL73: Revenue  | $  | 6,824  |    | $  | 4,634  |    | $  | 1,434  |\nL74: Gross margin  |    | 84  | %  |    | 79  | %  |    | 31  | %\nL75: Operating margin  |    | 79  | %  |    | 75  | %  |    | 20  | %\nL76: Business Outlook\nL77: \nL78: The following table presents Micron’s guidance for the first quarter of 2027:\nL79: \nL80: FQ1-27  | GAAP^{(1) }Outlook  | Non-GAAP^{(2) }Outlook\nL81:    |    |\nL82: Revenue  | $61.5 billion ± $1.5 billion  | $61.5 billion ± $1.5 billion\nL83: Gross margin  | Approximately 85.95%  | Approximately 86.25%\nL84: Operating expenses  | Approximately $2.31 billion  | Approximately $2.06 billion\nL85: Diluted earnings per share  | $37.84 ± $1.00  | $38.15 ± $1.00\nL86: Further information regarding Micron’s business outlook is included in the prepared remarks and slides, which have been posted at cite2†investors.micron.com .\nL87: \nL88: Product Highlights\nL89:   * We began sampling the industry's first 512GB ultra dense high-capacity DDR5 RDIMM modules capable of speeds up to 9,200 MT/s.\nL90:   * We have completed multiple customer qualifications of our 1-gamma based, 8,800 MT/s high-speed server RDIMM modules.\nL91:   * Our industry leading server LPDDR SOCAMM portfolio revenue more than doubled sequentially in the fourth quarter of 2026.\nL92:   * Our 7600 PCIe Gen 5 and 9650 PCIe Gen 6 SSD high-performance products are now shipping to market-leading customers for KV-cache applications.\nL93:   * Our 6600 ION SSD achieved a strong volume ramp in the fourth quarter of 2026.\nL94:   * We are now shipping 6-channel 1-gamma LPDDR5X for flagship mobile devices.\nL95:   * We have secured design wins with every Tier 1 OEM customer for AI workstation product.\nL96:   * Our 4600 SSD secured additional qualifications with leading PC OEMs.\nL97:   * We began sampling 1-gamma based LPDDR6 products to multiple physical AI markets.\nL98: Investor Webcast\nL99: \nL100: Micron will host a conference call on Wednesday, September 30, 2026 at 2:30 p.m. Mountain Time to discuss its fourth-quarter and full-year financial results and provide forward-looking guidance for its first quarter. A live webcast of the call will be available online at cite2†investors.micron.com . A webcast replay will be available for one year after the call.\nL101: We encourage you to visit our website at cite3†micron.com†micron.com throughout the quarter for the most current information on the company, including information on financial conferences that we may be attending. You can also follow us on LinkedIn, X (@MicronTech) and YouTube (@MicronTechnology).\nL102: \nL103: About Micron Technology, Inc.\nL104: Micron Technology, Inc. is a global leader in semiconductor memory and storage, powering AI and compute-intensive applications from cloud to edge. With a relentless focus on our customers, technology and product leadership, and manufacturing and operational excellence, Micron’s comprehensive portfolio of high-performance DRAM, NAND and NOR solutions deliver the speed, efficiency, and scale today’s workloads demand, accelerating intelligence to enrich life for all.\nL105: To learn more about Micron Technology, Inc. (Nasdaq: MU), visit micron.com.\nL106: © 2026 Micron Technology, Inc. All rights reserved. Micron, the Micron logo, and all other Micron trademarks are the property of Micron Technology, Inc. All other trademarks are the property of their respective owners.\nL107: \nL108: Forward-Looking Statements\nL109: This press release contains forward-looking statements regarding our industry, our strategic position, our customers, including customer demand, our investments and the goals for such investments, our business opportunity, our products and technology, and our financial and operating performance, including our guidance for the first quarter. These forward-looking statements are subject to a number of risks and uncertainties that could cause actual results to differ materially.\nL110: Please refer to the documents we file with the Securities and Exchange Commission, including our most recent Form 10-K and Form 10-Q. These documents contain and identify important factors that could cause our actual results to differ materially from those contained in these forward-looking statements. These certain factors can be found at investors.micron.com/risk-factor.\nL111: Although we believe that the expectations reflected in the forward-looking statements are reasonable, we cannot guarantee future results, levels of activity, performance, or achievements. We are under no duty to update any of the forward-looking statements to conform these statements to actual results.\nL112: ^{(1)}  | GAAP represents U.S. Generally Accepted Accounting Principles.\nL113: ^{(2)}  | Non-GAAP represents GAAP excluding the impact of certain activities, which management excludes in analyzing our operating results and understanding trends in our earnings; adjusted free cash flow; investments in capital expenditures, net; and business outlook. Further information regarding Micron’s use of non-GAAP measures and reconciliations between GAAP and non-GAAP measures are included within this press release.\nL114: MICRON TECHNOLOGY, INC.\nL115: CONSOLIDATED STATEMENTS OF OPERATIONS\nL116: (In millions, except per share amounts)\nL117: (Unaudited)\nL118:    | 4th Qtr.  | 3rd Qtr.  | 4th Qtr.  | Year Ended\nL119:    | September 3,\nL120: 2026  | May 28,\nL121: 2026  | August 28,\nL122: 2025  | September 3,\nL123: 2026  | August 28,\nL124: 2025\nL125:    |    |    |    |    |\nL126: